  "note": "ONEWAY1u (D194 point 6): what `daoris connect`, `retire`, `wire` and `import` said for each case of their tests, run once through the CLI's TypeScript verbs before they retire, over a stand-in service that answers as the row says (`service` and `reply`; the requests it was sent are `calls`) and a working tree of the row's files at `<root>`, named `engine`. A row of the `command` door is the verb's own grammar and its service address, held for the command tree's table. `DriverRegistryTextTests` reads it row for row; a sentence the port changes on purpose says why under `changed`.",
